# tools/ales_stereo_limit_env_hold_witness.rish — stereo_limit_env_hold: the attack/hold/release brickwall limiter carried into stereo, the linked held envelope driving one linked ceiling over time (ALES169).
#
# Season: the Six-Season double-seat, Season C thread (Lotus · the creative suite) · waymark ALES · rung ALES169.
# Design read: active-designing/date/20260815/20260815-073957_fill-ales169-lotus-stereo-limit-env-hold.md
# Stands on: lotus/stereo_hold_env.rye (ALES165 — the linked held follower, its stereo_env_step_hold reused whole), lotus/stereo_limit_env.rye (ALES163 — the un-held linked limiter this reduces to at a hold of zero),
# lotus/limit_env_hold.rye (ALES59 — the mono attack/hold/release limiter, its LimitEnvHoldError reused whole and its output the left-always-peak comparison), lotus/limit.rye (ALES49 — the ceiling), lotus/pan.rye
# (ALES10 — the StereoClip), lotus/timeline.rye (ALES2 — the Clip, sample_max, max_clip).
#
# lotus/stereo_limit_env_hold.rye limits a span of sample-PAIRS in a master to a magnitude ceiling, the one gain reduction following the shared LINKED HELD envelope over time. Each pair advances one shared envelope with one
# shared hold countdown toward the linked peak max(|left|, |right|) by ALES165's step (attack while rising and rearming the shared hold, the peak pinned while the countdown lasts, release once it expires): within the ceiling
# both pass byte for byte, above it the single gain ceil/e (in (0, 1), the divide always safe since e > ceil >= 1) is applied to both raw samples — one detector, one hold, one ceiling, the image held. The limiter is the
# compressor at an infinite ratio, so there is no ratio knob. LimitEnvHoldError (BadCeiling, BadCoeff, BadHold, BadRange) reused whole; the fusion adds no fault. Values only, never a length. The crux is the zero-hold law (a
# hold of zero reducing it to ALES163's stereo_limit_env byte for byte on both — the held rung's no-hold limit exactly the un-held one already proven), the linked-gain-over-time law (a left-always-peak master with left' equal
# to ALES59's mono limit_env_hold(left), the right scaled by the same fraction, the independent per-channel limit_env_hold differing), the image law (the shared gain preserving the L:R ratio, an out-of-phase pair returning
# still out of phase), the knob / no-pump laws (below the ceiling the identity, a nonzero hold keeping the reduction engaged across a duck rather than pumping), the carry law (a span in two pieces, the split mid-hold, equal to
# the whole once on both, env and hold_left carrying), and the sub-ceiling/silence/balance/atomicity/degenerate law.
#
# Run from the repository root:
#   rishi/bin/rishi run tools/ales_stereo_limit_env_hold_witness.rish

say "ales-stereo-limit-env-hold: Language EN — stereo_limit_env_hold limits a span of sample-pairs in a stereo master to a magnitude ceiling, the one gain reduction following the shared linked held envelope over time. Each pair advances one shared envelope with one shared hold countdown toward the linked peak (the max of the two channels' magnitudes, clamped to the rail): the attack fraction while it rises and rearms the shared hold, the peak pinned while the countdown lasts, the release only once it expires; where the held envelope sits within the ceiling both channels pass byte for byte, and where it rises above, the single gain (the ceiling over the envelope, in the open interval zero to one) is applied to both raw samples. A limiter is the compressor at an infinite ratio, so there is no ratio knob. It validates the ceiling, attack, release, hold, and span once against the shared length before any write, so a refusal never limits one channel and leaves the other torn. It writes values only, never a length, so the two channels leave balanced; the caller owns the envelope and the countdown across calls, so a span limited in two pieces equals the whole once even when the split falls mid-hold."
say "ales-stereo-limit-env-hold: Style Radiant — ALES163 carried the breathing limiter into stereo: one shared envelope pinning the linked peak to the ceiling as it crosses and easing off as it falls away, one gain applied to both channels so the image never lurches. Yet an un-held limiter still releases and re-engages on a brief duck below the ceiling between two loud passages — it pumps, and the ear hears the level move across the whole field at once. A real limiter carries a hold knob for exactly this: on a fall away from a peak, it pins the peak for a little while before the release begins, so the gain reduction stays engaged through the duck and the passage stays whole. ALES165 built that hold stage inside the linked follower and proved it once. This rung spends that proof: it drives ALES49's ceiling from the linked held envelope rather than the plain linked one — the same stereo limiter, now with the patience that keeps it from pumping the image. It is the stereo mirror of ALES59's held mono limiter, and the rung that makes the stereo held-dynamics quartet whole — gate, compressor, limiter, expander all reading ALES165's one proven held follower. Two proofs fused: the detector is the linked held follower (one shared envelope, one shared hold countdown pinning the linked peak across a fall so the two channels never release on different samples), and the gain is linked (one ceiling gain from the linked held envelope applied to both). The crux is six laws: the zero-hold law (a hold of zero making the linked held follower the plain linked follower, so this equals ALES163's stereo_limit_env byte for byte on both — the held rung's no-hold limit exactly the un-held rung already proven); the linked-gain-over-time law (a left-always-peak master with the left equal to ALES59's mono limit_env_hold of it byte for byte, the right scaled by the same fraction, the independent per-channel limit_env_hold genuinely differing); the image law (the shared gain preserving the left-to-right ratio, an out-of-phase pair returning still out of phase, no magnitude expanding and no sign flipping); the knob and no-pump laws (below the ceiling the identity everywhere, and a nonzero hold keeping the gain reduction engaged across a brief duck — the held magnitude no larger than the un-held one and strictly quieter at the duck, the pumping avoided); the carry law (a span limited in two pieces, the split mid-hold, equal to limiting the whole once, byte for byte on both); and the sub-ceiling, silence, balance, atomicity, and degenerate law (a master whose linked held envelope never crosses the ceiling passing byte for byte, silence staying silence, the lengths held, each of the four refusals leaving both channels untouched and balanced, count zero the identity on both)."
say "ales-stereo-limit-env-hold: Lens TAME — two bounded in-process i16 Clips (left, right) carrying one shared i64 envelope and one shared u32 hold countdown, one linked-peak comparison and at most one multiply-then-divide for the held envelope step (ALES165's proven stereo_env_step_hold) plus one per channel for the gain, all in i64 (the product of a magnitude and the ceiling at most 32768 times 32767 never overflowing), the gain ceiling over e in the open interval zero to one so every scaled magnitude is strictly below its input's and fits i16; the two channels enter balanced (the StereoClip invariant asserted on entry) and leave balanced (a limiter writes values only, each length asserted equal and within bound on exit, each written sign asserted held); the ceiling, both coefficients, the hold, and the span are validated once before either channel is mutated, so a refusal never limits one channel and leaves the other torn; on the above-ceiling branch the envelope is asserted strictly greater than the ceiling which is at least one, so the divide is always safe and the gain a genuine reduction; StereoLimitEnvHoldError is ALES59's LimitEnvHoldError (BadCeiling, BadCoeff, BadHold, BadRange) reused whole, the fusion adding no fault, and a limiter has no ratio knob so there is no BadRatio. The zero-hold law is proven by running both stereo_limit_env_hold under a hold of zero and ALES163's un-held stereo_limit_env on the same master and demanding byte-for-byte equality on both channels; the linked-gain-over-time law against a master where the left always holds the peak — the left equal to ALES59's mono limit_env_hold of it byte for byte while the right is scaled by the same fraction, the independent mono limit_env_hold of the right alone shown to genuinely differ; the image law proves no magnitude expands and no sign flips over a mixed master and that an out-of-phase pair returns still exactly out of phase; the knob and no-pump laws prove below the ceiling the identity everywhere and a nonzero hold keeping the reduction engaged across a duck where an un-held limiter pumps; the carry law proves a span limited in two pieces, the split mid-hold, equal to the whole once on both channels; and the sub-ceiling, silence, balance, atomicity, and degenerate cases prove a within-ceiling master passing byte for byte, an all-silent master staying zero, the length held, each of the four refusals leaving both channels untouched and balanced, and an empty span the identity on both; siloed to lotus/, the ceiling a magnitude in sample units, the attack, release, and hold per sample index, no lookahead, no real sample rate, no anti-aliasing, no network, no keys, no funds, no device, no speaker."

let zig = "vendor/zig-toolchain/zig"
let bin = "lotus/bin/stereo_limit_env_hold"

let build = run ["sh" "-c" "mkdir -p lotus/bin && env RYE_ZIG=${zig} rye/bin/rye build lotus/stereo_limit_env_hold.rye -femit-bin=${bin}"]
assert build.ok else "ales-stereo-limit-env-hold: build failed — ${build.err}"

let outfile = "lotus/bin/stereo_limit_env_hold.out"
let selftest = run ["sh" "-c" "${bin} selftest > ${outfile} 2>&1"]
assert selftest.ok else "ales-stereo-limit-env-hold: selftest exited non-zero — see ${outfile}"

let shown = run ["sh" "-c" "cat ${outfile}"]
say "ales-stereo-limit-env-hold: ${shown.out}"

let green = run ["sh" "-c" "grep -q 'GREEN ales-stereo-limit-env-hold' ${outfile} && echo yes"]
assert (trim green.out) == "yes" else "ales-stereo-limit-env-hold: selftest did not print the GREEN ales-stereo-limit-env-hold line"
